      "year": 2025,
      "abstract": "The article is devoted to a critical analysis of the main forms of the materialist interpre\u00adtation of Hegelian philosophy as speculative theology, which was first developed by L. Feuerbach and then developed by K. Marx and F. Engels. According to the main prin\u00adciples of this interpretation, Hegelian dialectical thinking refers to the activity of an ideal imaginary subject who is the cause of the entire material world. The article shows that the essential possibilities associated with the materialistic understanding of the basic prin\u00adciples of the Hegelian dialectical method were realized by V.I. Lenin, who, following the Marxist approach to understanding Hegel\u2019s philosophy, considered his Logic as the science of conceptually conceivable objective forms of being and the universal laws of development of all things. The Hegelian idea, expressing the dialectical identity of thought and being, appears to him not as a theological essence idealistically con\u00adstructed by thought, as Marx believed, but as an absolute real subject that should be thought of as matter, which manifests itself in the objective real being of nature in the same way as in the subjectivity of human thinking, cognizing this being.",
